# Marks of Trombone Copprash.pdf (the library's MobileSheets/ folder), read off the page by eye (2026-10-10).
# A heavy old plate-print scan: no notes in the PDF, so only the picture to go by.
#
# page 3 (0-based): staves 1-5 are No. 7 (slurs over groups, hairpins, dynamics), staves 6-11 are No. 8 (Tempo giusto).
# No. 8 in 3/4: runs of 16ths in groups of four - each group has a staccato dot on its FIRST note and a slur from its
# SECOND note to its FOURTH; a bar is 2 groups + an eighth + an eighth rest, or 3 groups.
#
#   bar <staff> <bar in that staff, from 0> <groups>      scored: staccato on notes 0,4,(8); slur from note 1 to 3, 5 to 7, (9 to 11)
#   dyn <staff> <letters left to right>                    dynamics on the staff, in order
#   hair <staff> <cresc|dim ...>                           hairpins on the staff, in order
#
# Rows of No. 8 left out of "bar" lines (staves 8, 9): their groups are not all the same (some have no dot or no slur).
file MobileSheets/Trombone Copprash.pdf
page 3
bar 6 0 2
bar 6 1 2
bar 6 2 3
bar 6 3 2
bar 7 0 3
bar 7 1 3
bar 7 2 3
bar 7 3 2
bar 10 0 3
bar 10 1 2
bar 10 2 3
bar 10 3 2
bar 11 0 2
bar 11 1 2
bar 11 2 3
bar 11 3 2
dyn 1 p p f
hair 1 cresc dim cresc dim
dyn 2 p p
hair 2 cresc dim cresc
dyn 3 p f
hair 3 dim dim
dyn 4 p p
hair 4 dim cresc dim cresc
dyn 5 f
hair 5 dim
dyn 6 p f
hair 6 dim
dyn 7 p f
dyn 8 p
hair 8 dim
dyn 9 f p f p
dyn 10 f
hair 10 cresc dim
dyn 11 p f
# Not scored: a group whose slur is hidden under a fingering figure.
skipslur 7 2 0
